.TH "YAMLR-BASELINE" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-baseline \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBSnapshot Current Violations to Ignore in Future Scans\fR
.PP
The \fBbaseline\fR command is a core component of the \fBGitOps Guard\fR strategy. It allows teams to adopt Yamlr on legacy codebases by "fingerprinting" all existing violations and saving them to a JSON file. Future scans can then use this file to ignore those specific issues, ensuring that only \fBnew\fR regressions block your CI/CD pipelines.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr baseline [PATH]... [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Scans your manifests and generates a \fB.yamlr-baseline.json\fR file (by default) containing SHA-256 fingerprints of every finding.
.PP
.SS "Fingerprint Integrity"
Fingerprints are generated based on:
.PP
1.  \fBRule ID\fR: The specific check that failed.
.PP
2.  \fBResource Identity\fR: The \fBkind\fR and \fBname\fR of the resource.
.PP
3.  \fBNormalized Path\fR: The workspace-relative path to the file.
.PP
4.  \fBMessage Context\fR: The specific error message.
.PP
.IP "\fBNOTE:\fR" 4
\fBLine numbers are excluded\fR from the fingerprint. This ensures that the baseline remains valid even if you add or remove lines elsewhere in the file.
.PP
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--output <PATH>\fR: Custom path for the baseline file (Default: \fB.yamlr-baseline.json\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--ext <EXTENSIONS>\fR: Extensions to process (Default: \fB.yaml,.yml\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--max-depth <N>\fR: Limit directory recursion.
.SH "HOW TO USE IN CI/CD (GITOPS GUARD)"
1.  \fBEstablish Baseline\fR: Run once on your main branch.
.PP
.nf
.RS
    yamlr baseline . --output .yamlr-baseline.json
    git add .yamlr-baseline.json && git commit -m "docs: establish yamlr baseline"
.RE
.fi
2.  \fBEnforce in PRs\fR: Use the \fB--baseline\fR flag in your PR checks.
.PP
.nf
.RS
    yamlr scan . --baseline .yamlr-baseline.json --fail-on any
.RE
.fi
Yamlr will return \fBexit code 0\fR (PASS) if all findings are in the baseline, and \fBexit code 1\fR (FAIL) only if a new violation is introduced.
.PP
.SS " Universal Expert Flags"
Available across primary commands:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Output surgical execution timing breakdown.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing-file <FILE>\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Save performance profiling data to a JSON file.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--verbose\fR\fR: Full audit logs and engine stages.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR: Minimal output mode (exit codes only).
